PCILeechGen failure catalogue
=============================

Run `sudo pcileechgen doctor --bdf <BDF>` before changing host security,
kernel, BIOS, VFIO, or firmware settings. A Windows Code 10 is a terminal
symptom; fix the first failed boundary below.

HOST-IOMMU-001 — IOMMU is not ready
  Evidence: required kernel parameter missing or no IOMMU groups exist.
  Action: enable intel_iommu=on or amd_iommu=on with iommu=pt, reboot, and
          verify /sys/kernel/iommu_groups. Do not use ACS override as a
          substitute for physical DMA isolation without understanding that it
          changes grouping, not hardware isolation.

HOST-BOOT-002 — live or overlay Linux root
  Evidence: root filesystem is overlay/squashfs.
  Action: use a persistent Linux installation for disruptive VFIO work.

VFIO-DRIVER-001 — donor is not bound to vfio-pci
  Action: use `pcileechgen vfio prepare`; retain its restoration state file.

VFIO-GROUP-001 — mixed IOMMU group
  Evidence: one or more group members remain on native drivers.
  Action: prepare the complete safe group or use a physically isolated slot.
          Never bind a root controller, active display, input controller, or
          default-route NIC merely to make the group viable.

POWER-D3-001 — donor is not in D0
  Action: inspect with `pcileechgen power status`; use `power wake` only when
          the device is not host-critical. Some donors require their native
          driver to initialize them before transfer to vfio-pci.

BAR-READ-FF-001 — mapped BAR samples are uniformly 0xFF
  Check in order: D0 state, group viability, mapping method, reset state,
                  native-driver initialization, PCIe AER/link errors.
  Do not diagnose a complete BAR from a single DWORD.

BAR-BRAM-002 — donor BAR exceeds board BRAM
  Action: use a smaller-aperture donor or a board with sufficient BRAM. Force
          mode truncates behavior and is not a compatibility fix.

VIVADO-ENV-001 / VIVADO-VERSION-001
  Action: verify the selected executable and supported version.

VIVADO-LICENSE-002
  Evidence: license environment is absent after privilege transition.
  Action: preserve XILINXD_LICENSE_FILE or LM_LICENSE_FILE through sudo.

VIVADO-XML-001
  Evidence: a named Vivado device XML file fails parsing.
  Action: repair or reinstall the affected device files. `--skip-vivado`
          separates generated-artifact correctness from synthesis failures.

FLASH-MANIFEST-005 — artifact differs from build manifest
  Action: stop. Rebuild or reflash only after `pcileechgen flash verify` passes.
  A board LED is not proof of complete or correct programming.

Windows Code 10
---------------
Collect bounded PnP evidence with:

  powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File tools/collect_device_diagnostics.ps1 \
    -HardwareId 'PCI\VEN_xxxx&DEV_xxxx'

Classify before cleanup:
  WIN-PNP-DRIVER-001     no matching driver
  WIN-PNP-RESOURCE-002   resource assignment failed
  WIN-PNP-START-003      driver initialization failed
  WIN-PNP-RESET-004      reset handshake timed out
  WIN-PNP-INTERRUPT-005  MSI/MSI-X initialization failed
  WIN-PNP-STALE-006      conflicting stale device instances

Use cleanup_device_history only for WIN-PNP-STALE-006. Do not disable Secure
Boot or Core Isolation as a generic response to incorrect BAR, reset, or
interrupt behavior.

xHCI status
-----------
xHCI initialization requires host-owned halted reset state, HCRST/CNR
sequencing, Run/Stop to HCHalted transitions, DCBAAP/CRCR/CONFIG programming,
command/event rings, doorbells, and interrupts. Enumeration alone does not
prove xHCI compatibility. Compare donor and emulator sessions with
`pcileechgen validate-init` and fix the first divergence.
